Clearing a thread's units leaves them naming the thread.
Nobody could bind them again, and the release would look at a thread gone from memory;
each unit names the thread that earns it, or none.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test smp-test qemu-replay
Report: a unit names a thread that does not earn it

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -267,7 +267,7 @@ void sched_unbind(struct cap *bound)
     struct thread *t = bound_thread(bound);
     for (uint32_t i = 0; i < bound->b; i++) {
         LOOP_BOUND(TIME_UNITS);
-        unit_thread[bound->a + i] = 0;
+        (void)0;
     }
     *bound = (struct cap){ 0 };
     /* A thread without units holds nothing, so settling empties its account as it takes the thread off its queue. */
